menu "kws-de inference"

config KWS_INFER_GENERATED
    bool "Use the generated inference runtime instead of the TFLite Micro interpreter"
    default y
    help
      Run the C generated by kws-codegen (firmware/main/gen/*_infer.c), which
      calls esp-nn's ESP32-S3 kernels directly, instead of dispatching through
      tflite::MicroInterpreter, for both the wake and the command model. The
      generated path is bit-exact with the interpreter
      (firmware/test/test_wake_smoke, firmware/test/test_command_smoke,
      firmware/test/test_wake_parity, firmware/test/test_command_parity,
      tests/test_codegen_parity.py).

      Turning this off restores the interpreter without touching any other
      code, which is the fallback if a newly exported model hits an op the
      generator refuses.

choice KWS_INFER_COMMAND_ARENA
    prompt "Where the generated command model's arena lives"
    depends on KWS_INFER_GENERATED
    default KWS_INFER_COMMAND_ARENA_PSRAM
    help
      gen/command_infer.c's arena is 51,248 B — one static array, so this is a
      link-time choice, not an allocation. The wake model's 15,680 B arena is
      always internal: it is small, and it runs every 30 ms.

config KWS_INFER_COMMAND_ARENA_PSRAM
    bool "PSRAM (.ext_ram.bss)"
    help
      The default. 51 KB of internal SRAM is more than this device has to
      spare: claiming it unconditionally starved the recognise, record and
      console task stacks, which must be internal and cannot be moved. Costs
      ~1.4 ms of the ~28 ms evaluation (the interpreter ran its arena from
      PSRAM too, so this is still ~1.5x faster than the interpreter path).

config KWS_INFER_COMMAND_ARENA_INTERNAL
    bool "Internal SRAM (.bss)"
    help
      ~1.4 ms faster, and 51,248 B of internal SRAM gone. Only viable in a
      build that is not also creating the record/console tasks — it is the
      measurement configuration, not a shipping one. If tasks stop being
      created, this is why: look for "not created: free internal ..." in the
      boot log.

endchoice

config KWS_INFER_PARITY_LOG
    bool "Log generated-vs-interpreter output once per mode entry"
    depends on KWS_INFER_GENERATED
    default n
    help
      On the first step after entering a mode, run both paths on the same input
      and log the two outputs side by side: proof that they still agree on real
      device audio.

      It is off by default because it keeps the whole interpreter in the build
      — including the 40 KB wake tensor arena it takes out of internal RAM and
      the 64 KB command arena in PSRAM, which is most of what generating the
      inference was for. Treat it as a developer-verification switch: turn it
      on, confirm "parity: out byte generated N, interpreter N" (wake) and
      "parity: 0/23 output bytes differ" (command), turn it off to ship. With
      it off both models run on the generated code alone: no MicroInterpreter,
      no resource variables, no tensor arenas.

      It needs KWS_INFER_COMMAND_ARENA_PSRAM (the default) to get as far as
      printing the command line at all: with the arena in internal SRAM there
      is not enough left to create the recognise task. Even with PSRAM this
      build is short enough that the record task does not start — measured,
      logged as "record task (8192 B stack) not created", and acceptable
      because verifying parity needs only wake and recognise. If a task is
      missing, that log line says so.

endmenu
